E AX3064 644-parallel-thunk-shape.ax:46:34-35 parallel-capture "a concurrent binding captures `s`, which has type `String` - a reference the parent also holds" #"`s` is bound outside this binding" !"MM-PAR-6: a binding runs BESIDE its parent, and `axiom_retain`/`axiom_release` are a plain load-add-store rather than an `atomicrmw` - two threads touching one block's count lose an increment and free a block a live reference still names. The rule is the language's and not the lowering's, so it does not depend on `--threads`; `__proc_spawn` names the isolated lowering and is exempt" ?"pass the value in through the thunk's word argument instead of capturing it, or build a copy of it inside the binding. A `parallel` binding may borrow a `String` its parent holds; anything else it shares with its parent is a word. To share other read-only input with several workers, use `stdlib/Par.ax`, whose forked children read their own copy"
E AX3064 644-parallel-thunk-shape.ax:55:29-31 parallel-capture "a concurrent binding spawns a call result, whose captures this checker cannot see" #"the thunk's captures are not visible here" !"MM-PAR-6: a binding runs BESIDE its parent, and `axiom_retain`/`axiom_release` are a plain load-add-store rather than an `atomicrmw` - two threads touching one block's count lose an increment and free a block a live reference still names. The rule is the language's and not the lowering's, so it does not depend on `--threads`; `__proc_spawn` names the isolated lowering and is exempt" ?"write the lambda at the spawn, or name a top-level function: a literal is checked where it stands and a top-level name captures nothing"
E AX3064 644-parallel-thunk-shape.ax:65:32-33 parallel-capture "a concurrent binding spawns a field, whose captures this checker cannot see" #"the thunk's captures are not visible here" !"MM-PAR-6: a binding runs BESIDE its parent, and `axiom_retain`/`axiom_release` are a plain load-add-store rather than an `atomicrmw` - two threads touching one block's count lose an increment and free a block a live reference still names. The rule is the language's and not the lowering's, so it does not depend on `--threads`; `__proc_spawn` names the isolated lowering and is exempt" ?"write the lambda at the spawn, or name a top-level function: a literal is checked where it stands and a top-level name captures nothing"
